    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "gentle acts of presence... it just feels like pretending. like i'm just waiting for a train that isn't coming. i look at my hands and i dont even recognize them. they used to be so useful, so decisive. now they're just... idle. it feels wrong to keep carrying around a body that has nothing left to do. like it's just a burden i'm dragging around for no reason.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
